%1 must log out of Linux and back in before this takes full effect.\n\nSD sees the change at once - its gates read /etc/group on every call, so login\nand logto will admit %1 straight away. The filesystem does not: the account's\nfiles belong to its group, and a Linux session keeps the groups it held when it\nstarted, so until %1 logs in again they can enter the account but cannot\nchange anything in it.\n\nThe same is true of revoke, where it matters more: somebody whose grant has\nbeen taken away can still change the account's files until their next login,\neven though SD has already stopped admitting them.
